  "name": "Question 11",
  "problem": "What are the minimum and maximum of the set $A=\\{n\\in R∣\\,5<n\\le 9\\}?$\n\nThe minimum of the set {{field-1}}, while the maximum of the set {{field-2}}.",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that \n\n- ${x}_{max}$ is the maximum of a set $S$ if ${x}_{max}\\in S$ and $x\\le {x}_{max}$ for all $x\\in S,$ and\n\n- ${x}_{min}$ is the minimum of a set $S$ if ${x}_{min}\\in S$ and $x\\ge {x}_{min}$ for all $x\\in S.$\n\nNotice that $A=(5,9],$ where $5\\notin A.$ So, we have the following:\n\n- $min(A)=min(5,9],$ which $\\text{does not exist}$\n\n- $max(A)=min(5,9]=9$",
